  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37571208",
      "title": "Signals: What & Why?",
      "lectureOrder": 675,
      "videoOrder": 621,
      "sourceHash": "3eddf141274c914cf306f10290eee5184e35a73da67d5b0ff59613d62d37e5c7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.745,
          "end": 4.394,
          "en": "So what's the purpose of signals?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.394,
          "end": 7.865,
          "en": "In the end, signals give us an Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.865,
          "end": 10.749,
          "en": "a new way of handling data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.749,
          "end": 13.377,
          "en": "and of updating the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.377,
          "end": 16.989,
          "en": "Without signals, so without this new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.989,
          "end": 20.007,
          "en": "Angular relies on its classic change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.007,
          "end": 22.739,
          "en": "detection algorithm for finding out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.739,
          "end": 24.245,
          "en": "whether some data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.245,
          "end": 26.884,
          "en": "and the UI should be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.884,
          "end": 29.026,
          "en": "You will also sometimes hear of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.026,
          "end": 33.141,
          "en": "referred to as zone based change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.141,
          "end": 34.248,
          "en": "because under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.248,
          "end": 37.359,
          "en": "this classic change detection algorithm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.359,
          "end": 40.908,
          "en": "uses a library called zone.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.908,
          "end": 43.753,
          "en": "In a typical Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.753,
          "end": 47.89,
          "en": "like this one here, data is changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.89,
          "end": 50.523,
          "en": "by simply defining class properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.523,
          "end": 52.75,
          "en": "and by changing those properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.75,
          "end": 56.009,
          "en": "for example, in methods that are triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.009,
          "end": 59.236,
          "en": "once buttons are pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.236,
          "end": 61.232,
          "en": "That data like this counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.232,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "or this list of actions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 65.129,
          "en": "can then be output in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.129,
          "end": 66.752,
          "en": "by using template bindings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.752,
          "end": 69.018,
          "en": "like these double curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.018,
          "end": 72.251,
          "en": "So by using string interpolation, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.251,
          "end": 74.396,
          "en": "That's Angular as you know it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.396,
          "end": 77.401,
          "en": "And here, I'm using a standalone component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.401,
          "end": 78.23400000000001,
          "en": "but the code, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.23400000000001,
          "end": 80.261,
          "en": "would be exactly the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.261,
          "end": 83.388,
          "en": "if I were using NgModules here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.388,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "This is how you manage and change data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 89.502,
          "en": "Now, the advantage of this classic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.502,
          "end": 91.145,
          "en": "change detection approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.145,
          "end": 92.731,
          "en": "which is actually the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.731,
          "end": 94.989,
          "en": "change detection approach in Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.989,
          "end": 98.003,
          "en": "and which until Angular 16",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.003,
          "end": 100.25200000000001,
          "en": "where signals were added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.25200000000001,
          "end": 103.244,
          "en": "was the only change detection approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.244,
          "end": 106.375,
          "en": "is that changes are detected automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.375,
          "end": 109.50800000000001,
          "en": "and the UI is then updated automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.50800000000001,
          "end": 112.49600000000001,
          "en": "Because of this zone.js library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.49600000000001,
          "end": 115.512,
          "en": "which is used behind the scenes by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.512,
          "end": 117.646,
          "en": "Angular basically finds out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 117.646,
          "end": 120.633,
          "en": "when these methods are executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.633,
          "end": 122.236,
          "en": "To be precise, it finds out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.236,
          "end": 124.497,
          "en": "when a click occurs and it knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 124.497,
          "end": 127.128,
          "en": "that you're listening to click events here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.128,
          "end": 128.391,
          "en": "and it knows which methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.391,
          "end": 130.749,
          "en": "are executed up on clicks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 130.749,
          "end": 132.974,
          "en": "and it therefore then simply watches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 132.974,
          "end": 134.746,
          "en": "those methods you could see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 134.746,
          "end": 137.152,
          "en": "and it sees which data you're changing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 137.152,
          "end": 138.516,
          "en": "and it therefore knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 138.516,
          "end": 140.389,
          "en": "that the data has changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.389,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "once one of these buttons has been pressed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 145.987,
          "en": "and it then goes ahead and updates the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 145.987,
          "end": 148.25,
          "en": "so that the latest state of your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 148.25,
          "end": 150.505,
          "en": "is reflected on the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 150.505,
          "end": 154.251,
          "en": "And that's why as we press those buttons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 154.251,
          "end": 156.508,
          "en": "the UI is being updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 156.508,
          "end": 160.25,
          "en": "Angular with its classic change detection algorithm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 160.25,
          "end": 162.244,
          "en": "is taking care about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 162.244,
          "end": 163.262,
          "en": "Now, I don't know about you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 163.262,
          "end": 165.641,
          "en": "but I would say that this current",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 165.641,
          "end": 168.004,
          "en": "classic change detection approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 168.004,
          "end": 170.357,
          "en": "sounds pretty perfect, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 170.357,
          "end": 173.142,
          "en": "Everything happens automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 173.142,
          "end": 175.505,
          "en": "Well, that is of course good,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 175.505,
          "end": 178.01,
          "en": "but the downside is that the overall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 178.01,
          "end": 181.022,
          "en": "application performance could be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 181.022,
          "end": 183.262,
          "en": "and the bundle size could be smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 183.262,
          "end": 187.506,
          "en": "It is increased because of this zone.js library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 187.506,
          "end": 190.26,
          "en": "that's being used for change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 190.26,
          "end": 192.649,
          "en": "And since Angular has to watch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 192.649,
          "end": 194.356,
          "en": "for all those changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 194.356,
          "end": 196.628,
          "en": "and has to check all your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 196.628,
          "end": 199.629,
          "en": "and update the UI whenever anything happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 199.629,
          "end": 201.246,
          "en": "that could potentially lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 201.246,
          "end": 203,
          "en": "to a change in data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 203,
          "end": 206.02,
          "en": "the overall app performance is not optimal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 206.02,
          "end": 207.977,
          "en": "and that's the disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 207.977,
          "end": 211.003,
          "en": "of the current change detection approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 211.003,
          "end": 213.398,
          "en": "Application performance could be better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 213.398,
          "end": 215.01,
          "en": "And the bundle size,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 215.01,
          "end": 216.883,
          "en": "the overall application bundle size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 216.883,
          "end": 219.873,
          "en": "is actually increased because you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 219.873,
          "end": 222.02,
          "en": "to include that extra library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 222.02,
          "end": 226.108,
          "en": "that takes care about this change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 226.108,
          "end": 229.15800000000002,
          "en": "And that's where signals come in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 229.15800000000002,
          "end": 231.383,
          "en": "Signals give us an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.383,
          "end": 235.406,
          "en": "of managing and detecting those changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 235.406,
          "end": 237.877,
          "en": "and they allow Angular to get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237.877,
          "end": 240.249,
          "en": "of that extra library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 240.249,
          "end": 243.149,
          "en": "They allow Angular to stop watching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 243.149,
          "end": 244.893,
          "en": "your entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 244.893,
          "end": 247.002,
          "en": "and they therefore can lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 247.002,
          "end": 251.209,
          "en": "to better performance and a smaller bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 251.209,
          "end": 252.499,
          "en": "Because with signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 252.499,
          "end": 255.155,
          "en": "there is no automatic change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 255.155,
          "end": 257.25,
          "en": "Instead, you ask the developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 257.25,
          "end": 261.48,
          "en": "basically tell Angular when data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 261.48,
          "end": 263.023,
          "en": "and you also tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 263.023,
          "end": 265.382,
          "en": "where the data is being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 265.382,
          "end": 267.751,
          "en": "Therefore, Angular then also knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 267.751,
          "end": 270.496,
          "en": "which parts of the UI need to be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 270.496,
          "end": 272.506,
          "en": "when that data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 272.506,
          "end": 274.767,
          "en": "and that only those parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 274.767,
          "end": 277.507,
          "en": "of the UI have to be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 277.507,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "And therefore, you as a developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 281.638,
          "en": "have slightly more work to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 281.638,
          "end": 284.906,
          "en": "But as a big upside, as a big advantage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 284.906,
          "end": 287.247,
          "en": "you have full control and you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 287.247,
          "end": 290.013,
          "en": "very likely achieve a better performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 290.013,
          "end": 293.494,
          "en": "and get a smaller application bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 293.494,
          "end": 295.26,
          "en": "And that's why signals were added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 295.26,
          "end": 297.884,
          "en": "and why you could consider using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 297.884,
          "end": 299.484,
          "en": "Though I will already say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 299.484,
          "end": 301.384,
          "en": "that the bundle size improvement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 301.384,
          "end": 304.009,
          "en": "and also the performance improvement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 304.009,
          "end": 306.865,
          "en": "will only really be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 306.865,
          "end": 309.135,
          "en": "once signals are stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 309.135,
          "end": 311.249,
          "en": "and only if you then fully switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 311.249,
          "end": 313.495,
          "en": "to signals in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 313.495,
          "end": 315.997,
          "en": "As long as you have at least one component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 315.997,
          "end": 319.23199999999997,
          "en": "that relies on the old change detection approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 319.23199999999997,
          "end": 320.25,
          "en": "Angular, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 320.25,
          "end": 322.114,
          "en": "can't get rid of that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 322.114,
          "end": 323.881,
          "en": "And therefore, you then won't get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 323.881,
          "end": 325.752,
          "en": "too many benefits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 325.752,
          "end": 327.89,
          "en": "And at the moment with version 16,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 327.89,
          "end": 331.252,
          "en": "you also can't fully switch to signals yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 331.252,
          "end": 333.39300000000003,
          "en": "But in the future, you will be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 333.39300000000003,
          "end": 335.999,
          "en": "to get those extra benefits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 335.999,
          "end": 338.913,
          "en": "But how do those signals work now?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
